  "summary": "I added a \"Tour\" button in a bar under the canvas, outside it. It typechecks, builds and renders with no errors, and the screenshot shows the button below the canvas. I haven't clicked it or run a tour end to end, so the 3-second timing and the return to the overview are untested.\n\nClicking \"Tour\" focuses Mercury, then each planet outward to Neptune, about 3 seconds apiece, with the info panel showing for each. After Neptune the camera returns to the overview. While the tour runs the button reads \"Stop tour\", and clicking it, or pressing Escape, ends the tour and returns to the overview.\n\n`window.__TASK_STATE__` now includes `touring: boolean`.\n\nI made one choice you didn't specify: a manual click on the canvas, `__focusPlanet` or `__unfocus` also cancels the tour, so manual focus takes over from the tour."
